 There are Ayaat(آيات) in Qur'an that were revealed talking specifically about the Yahood(يهود).

43
00:04:23,021 --> 00:04:30,593
They were upset, from the outstart of the arrival of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Madina.

44
00:04:31,914 --> 00:04:40,416
And we can sense that from the conversation that occurred with two of the leaders of Al-Yahood(اليهود) in Madina

45
00:04:40,737 --> 00:04:43,457
Huyaye Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) and his brother Abu Yasir(أبوياسر).

46
00:04:44,979 --> 00:04:51,998
Safiyyah رضي الله عنها , the wife of Rasool Allah ﷺ, she says;

47
00:04:52,427 --> 00:04:59,523
 None of the children of my father or my uncle were more popular with them, both than I was.

48
00:04:59,763 --> 00:05:05,595
She's referring to her popularity with her father and her uncle, Abu Yasir(أبوياسر).

49
00:05:06,835 --> 00:05:14,259
She said: None of the children of my father or my uncle were more popular with them, both than I was.

50
00:05:15,011 --> 00:05:20,267
Whatever child of theirs wanted their attention, it was always me they put first.

51
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:22,754
When the Messenger of Allah came to Quba'a(قباء)

52
00:05:23,051 --> 00:05:25,066
the village of Bannu Amr Bin Auf(بنو عمرو بن عوف),

53
00:05:25,422 --> 00:05:28,982
my father and my uncle Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) went to him early in the morning

54
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,994
and only returned at sunset.

55
00:05:31,516 --> 00:05:36,026
So tired out, they could scarcely walk staggering from exhaustion.

56
00:05:37,102 --> 00:05:46,256
So, here we're dealing with an event that occurred on the first day of the arrival of Rasool Allah ﷺ to Madina.

57
00:05:46,347 --> 00:05:48,825
he is still in the outskirts of Madina, he's in Quba'a(قباء).

58
00:05:51,298 --> 00:05:56,531
Safiyyah(صفيه) says, they came back that day, tired and worn out.

59
00:05:57,938 --> 00:06:01,210
She said, I raised over to greet them, as was my custom,

60
00:06:01,290 --> 00:06:04,995
but I swear neither so much as looked at me

61
00:06:05,545 --> 00:06:10,855
I heard my uncle Abu Yasir(ابو ياسر) asked my father is that, he then?

62
00:06:11,813 --> 00:06:15,826
So she, First of all, she's saying that they neglected me.

63
00:06:15,866 --> 00:06:18,849
Obviously they were preoccupied with something else,

64
00:06:19,404 --> 00:06:20,792
none of them picked her up,

65
00:06:21,221 --> 00:06:23,779
and then she started hearing their conversation.

66
00:06:24,501 --> 00:06:28,845
Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) is asking, Huyaye(حيئي) and said: Is that, he then?

67
00:06:29,157 --> 00:06:32,789
He is talking about Muhammadﷺ, he's asking, is he the Prophet?

68
00:06:33,104 --> 00:06:34,997
Is he the one mentioned in our books?

69
00:06:35,302 --> 00:06:38,124
Is he the one prophesized by our Rabbis?

70
00:06:38,697 --> 00:06:40,083
So, is that he then.?

71
00:06:40,545 --> 00:06:43,229
Huyaye(حيئي) said; Yes, I swear by Allah.

72
00:06:44,364 --> 00:06:47,995
Abu Yasir(ابو ياسر) said: You recognize him from his character and description then?

73
00:06:48,413 --> 00:06:51,150
Huyaye(حيئي) said: I certainly do, in the name of Allah.

74
00:06:52,105 --> 00:06:55,095
Abu Yasir(ابوياسر) goes, so how will you relate to him?

75
00:06:55,787 --> 00:06:59,611
If he's a prophet? What does that mean, how will you respond to him?

76
00:07:00,132 --> 00:07:02,245
Look at what Huyaye Ibn Akhtab(حيئي إبن أخطب) said, he said;

77
00:07:02,635 --> 00:07:07,576
By Allah, I will be his enemy for as long as I live.

78
00:07:08,398 --> 00:07:09,142
Subhaan Allah-Hil-Azeem(سُبْحَان الله العظيم),

79
00:07:10,305 --> 00:07:13,364
so first, you recognize that he is the Prophet of Allah

80
00:07:13,488 --> 00:07:15,864
and you know for sure that he's a prophet of Allah.

81
00:07:16,281 --> 00:07:18,081
Rather than saying that I'm going to follow him,

82
00:07:18,430 --> 00:07:21,158
you say, you will be his enemy for the rest of your life.

83
00:07:21,388 --> 00:07:22,182
Why?

84
00:07:22,971 --> 00:07:24,216
Well, the reason is clear.

85
00:07:24,568 --> 00:07:26,142
It is because of envy,

86
00:07:26,358 --> 00:07:30,550
and Huyaye(حيئي) is jealous that

87
00:07:30,832 --> 00:07:33,754
 the Prophet ended up being an Arab rather than a Jew.

88
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:41,707
And this envy caused him to disbelief Rasool Allah ﷺ.

89
00:07:42,023 --> 00:07:44,612
And here we'll dealing with the worst type of kuffr(كفر)

90
00:07:44,941 --> 00:07:49,084
