109
00:09:02,303 --> 00:09:05,075
These were people, who were enemies of each other.

110
00:09:05,109 --> 00:09:09,052
Now, because of Islam, they were united, they were one.

111
00:09:09,905 --> 00:09:13,271
So, this Jewish man wasn't very happy.

112
00:09:13,446 --> 00:09:14,319
And he said;

113
00:09:14,637 --> 00:09:22,073
قَدِجْتَمَعَ مَلَاءُ بَنِيْ قَيْلَهْ بِهَذِهِ الْبِلَادْ لَا وَللَّهِ مَا لَنَا مَعَ هُمْ اِذَجْتَمَعَ مَلَاءَهُمْ بِهَا مِنْ قَرَارْ

114
00:09:22,423 --> 00:09:28,783
He said, the Al-Aos and Al-Khazraj(ألاوس والخزرج) are united in this land.

115
00:09:29,172 --> 00:09:33,767
And In the name of Allah, we have no place here, as long as they are united.

116
00:09:34,363 --> 00:09:40,620
Our survival as Jews in Madina is based on the disunity of the Arabs.

117
00:09:41,034 --> 00:09:45,184
And as long as they are united, we are at risk.

118
00:09:46,259 --> 00:09:48,725
So, he tells a young Jewish man,

119
00:09:48,768 --> 00:09:51,897
who was sitting with Al-Aos and Al-Khazraj(ألاوس والخزرج) in the same gathering

120
00:09:52,096 --> 00:09:56,197
to start reminding them about their days of war,

121
00:09:56,621 --> 00:09:59,796
bring up the day of Buath(بعاث), bring up the Battle of so and so,

122
00:09:59,868 --> 00:10:02,661
bring up the Battle of so and so, narrate some of that poetry

